WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
A route has five moves, each right or up. RRRRR misses the goal. RRRUU reaches it.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
At each move, every branch splits in two. After five moves the tree has 32 leaves.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:25.000
RRRRR, RRRRU and RRRUR miss. The budget runs out with 29 routes still untested.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:37.000
The branches fold into six endpoints. Ten different routes reach the square three steps right and two steps up.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:46.000
RURUR takes four turns. RRRUU takes one. Two of the ten valid routes tie for the fewest turns.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Right-only routes stay on the bottom row. Adding an up move makes the goal reachable.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Nine interval programs are tested on all 256 byte values. Only 48 ≤ b < 160 matches on every input.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:15.000
The new goal is five steps right and three up. Those move counts construct a route directly.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:23.000
Routes must reach a goal, proofs must derive a claim, and programs must meet a specification.
